          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Heyting category
            (called a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logos"} logos
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"} Freyd-Scedrov
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            in which each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:Sub(Y)\to Sub(X)
            has a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f
            (the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
            that exists in any
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+hyperdoctrine"} first-order hyperdoctrine
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+poset"} subobject poset
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sub
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi HeytAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sub}:\mathcal{C}^{op} \to HeytAlg
          %p
            It follows that each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            and the base-change functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            are Heyting algebra homomorphisms. The Heyting implication can be defined as follows: if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are subobjects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A\Rightarrow B) \in Sub(X)
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_i(A\cap B) \hookrightarrow X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon A\hookrightarrow X
            is the subobject inclusion and we take
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B\in Sub(A)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            which is full (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"}> typed
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first-order
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f
            provided by the above axiom gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            in this logic. On the other hand, any category defined in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            which satisfies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+separation"} bounded separation
            is a Heyting category.
          %p
            A
            %strong Heyting functor
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+functor"} coherent functor
            between Heyting categories which additionally preserves the right adjoints
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal interpretation
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order logic
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitary+coherent+category"} infinitary coherent category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
            is also a Heyting category.
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            preserve
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pi-pretopos"} Pi-pretopos
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+pretopos"} Heyting pretopos
          %p
            In particular, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+truncations"} propositional truncations
            form a Heyting category.
